entry.summary:
I found a small but visible UI bug on Claude's download page, claude.ai/download. Direct visit: the page detects your operating system and shows the matching download options. Arriving from another page (for example claude.ai/downloads, then "Download for Linux"): the OS check doesn't run. Every platform's button is shown, and the "Windows (arm64)" and "macOS" buttons render on top of each other.
Open claude.ai/downloads Click "Download for Linux" Look at the download buttons on claude.ai/download Seen in Chrome on Fedora Linux. My guess: the OS detection only runs on a full page load, so an in-app navigation renders the fallback "all platforms" layout, and that layout was never checked with all five buttons visible at once.
